# Web-only build context for apps/web/Dockerfile (context: repository root).
# BuildKit's per-Dockerfile ignore file (`<dockerfile>.dockerignore`, beside
# the Dockerfile) REPLACES the root `.dockerignore` for this build; nothing
# from the root file applies here. This file stands alone.
#
# It admits only the pnpm workspace root manifests and the three
# pnpm-workspace.yaml package trees: apps/web, packages/web-contract and
# modules/*/web. There are deliberately no parent re-includes (`!apps/`,
# `!modules/`, ...): Docker matches every pattern against each of a path's
# parent directories too, so re-including a parent re-includes its whole
# subtree, and that would pull every Python app, package and module back in.
**
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!apps/web
!apps/web/**
!packages/web-contract
!packages/web-contract/**
!modules/*/web
!modules/*/web/**

# Re-exclude private artifacts, local dependencies and build output inside the
# allowed trees (last match wins). Directory names are excluded at the
# directory level as well as by contents, so the directory entry itself never
# reaches the context either (`**/x/**` alone still leaves an empty `x`).
**/node_modules
**/node_modules/**
**/.next
**/.next/**
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/next-env.d.ts
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.envrc*
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.log
**/AGENTS.md
**/AGENTS.override.md
**/CLAUDE.md
**/CLAUDE.local.md
**/.mcp.json
**/rheo.local.*
**/.claude
**/.claude/**
**/.codex
**/.codex/**
**/.bureau
**/.bureau/**
**/.bureau-worktrees
**/.bureau-worktrees/**
**/.secrets
**/.secrets/**
**/.rheo-local
**/.rheo-local/**
**/.git
**/.git/**
**/.venv
**/.venv/**
private
**/private
**/private/**
